<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cepeda (1820)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1820</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentine-civil-wars">Argentine Civil Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cepeda of 1 February 1820 was fought in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> between the federalist caudillos <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Francisco Ramírez</a> of Entre Ríos and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estanislao-lopez">Estanislao López</a> of Santa Fe and the army of the Directory of the United Provinces. The federalist victory brought down the central government and was followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pilar">Treaty of Pilar</a>, opening a period of autonomous provinces.</p></div>
